# The packages every mos image carries, whatever board it is built for and
# whatever the build declines. Nothing here is selectable: a root with no
# mos-system has no state mounts, no seed and reconcile tools and no operator
# account, and a root with no mos-ca-trust cannot verify a TLS peer.
mos-system
mos-ca-trust

# The emergency binary, and it is in `common` rather than a feature set on
# purpose. Every other manifest family is declinable -- a feature can be left
# out with --without, a radio with the board that has none -- and a tool an
# operator reaches for when the normal userland is damaged is worth nothing if
# the image in their hands is the build that declined it. It costs one 830 KB
# file, it enables nothing, nothing depends on it, and it changes no PATH; the
# whole of it is /usr/bin/busybox, reached by naming an applet.
mos-busybox
